          "screenshot_evidence": "The screenshot shows a Coursera course/program page titled \u201cGoogle Project Management Professional Certificate\u201d with the Google logo above the title. Beneath the title, it shows \u201cInstructor: Google Career Certificates.\u201d There is a large blue button \u201cEnroll for free\u201d and text \u201c2,809,447 already enrolled.\u201d The page breadcrumb area shows \u201cBrowse > Business > Leadership and Management.\u201d The screenshot does not show an explicit \u201cBeginner\u201d label, a numeric star rating, or an estimated duration. On the right side there is a chat/privacy panel (\u201cYour privacy and this chat\u2026 Got it\u201d) and a section titled \u201cIs this right for me?\u201d with prompt buttons including \u201cI have no experience. Can I keep up?\u201d",
          "criterion_analysis": "Partial success. The agent has opened and identified a relevant project-management offering, and the title/provider are clearly visible (Google / Google Career Certificates). However, the criterion asks for a \u201cbeginner-appropriate\u201d result; while the screenshot includes a prompt about having no experience, it does not explicitly display the level (e.g., \u201cBeginner\u201d), so beginner suitability is not fully confirmed from this screenshot alone. Still, it is clearly a project-management certificate and the first result page is open, so partial credit is warranted.",
          "discrepancies": "The agent\u2019s predicted output claims the page/DOM does not expose key metadata like rating/duration/level; the screenshot indeed does not show rating/duration/level, but it does show clear title and provider (\u201cInstructor: Google Career Certificates\u201d), which the agent also acknowledged. No contradiction on the first-result identification; the only mismatch is that the agent did not leverage the visible \u201cI have no experience. Can I keep up?\u201d as supporting evidence of beginner-friendliness (though it still isn\u2019t an explicit level tag).",
          "environment_issues_confirmed": false,
