        {
          "screenshot_evidence": "The screenshot shows a Coursera course/program page titled at the top-left: \u201cGoogle Project Management Professional Certificate\u201d with a Google \u201cG\u201d logo. The navigation tabs \u201cAbout\u201d, \u201cOutcomes\u201d, \u201cCourses\u201d, and \u201cTestimonials\u201d are visible. In the main content area, a section header reads \u201cPrepare for a career as a Project Manager\u201d with bullet points including: \u201cReceive professional-level training from Google\u201d, \u201cDemonstrate your technical proficiency\u201d, \u201cEarn an employer-recognized certificate from Google\u201d, and \u201cPrepare for an industry certification exam.\u201d On the right side there is a chat/privacy panel titled \u201cYour privacy and this chat\u201d with a \u201cGot it\u201d button, and below it a section titled \u201cIs this right for me?\u201d with suggested questions like \u201cHow does this compare to individual courses?\u201d and \u201cWill employers take this certificate seriously?\u201d No search results list is visible; only this single program page is shown. The provider \u201cGoogle\u201d is clearly indicated by the title and the bullet text mentioning Google.",
          "criterion_analysis": "This criterion requires opening one beginner-appropriate project-management course result and identifying its title and provider. The screenshot clearly shows that a Coursera result page is open for \u201cGoogle Project Management Professional Certificate,\u201d and the provider is Google (shown by the Google logo/branding and multiple mentions of Google in the page content). While the screenshot does not explicitly show a \u201cBeginner\u201d label, it does confirm the agent opened a relevant project-management offering and the title/provider are clear. Therefore, the evidence supports satisfying the criterion (opening the first result and identifying title/provider).",
          "discrepancies": "The agent\u2019s predicted output claims that only provider=Google is \u201cconcrete\u201d and that rating/duration/level are not visible; this is consistent with the screenshot (no rating/duration/level is shown in the visible area). However, the predicted output implies difficulty extracting title/provider; the screenshot actually makes the title (\u201cGoogle Project Management Professional Certificate\u201d) and provider (Google) plainly visible. Also, the predicted output suggests headings like \u201cDetails to know\u201d are visible; in this screenshot, \u201cDetails to know\u201d text is not visible\u2014only \u201cPrepare for a career as a Project Manager\u201d and the right-side chat panel are visible.",
