    "step8_outcome_verification": {
      "primary_intent": "The user wanted the agent, starting on Coursera, to find beginner-friendly project management courses, open two specific course result pages, extract key comparable attributes (provider, rating, estimated duration, level, skills), and then recommend the shorter option that is still well-rated\u2014without enrolling. A reasonable user would be flexible on which two beginner PM courses are chosen, but not flexible on missing the two-course comparison, omitting the required attributes, or failing to provide the final recommendation.",
      "reasoning": "Nitpicks: Not explicitly showing the very first moment on the Coursera homepage is minor because later evidence shows Coursera homepage access and on-site search with a Beginner filter applied; also, not providing a URL is not required by the task.\n\nCritical issues: (1) The agent opened only one course page (Google Project Management Professional Certificate) and never opened a second result page. Screenshots show multiple alternative results available on the search results page (e.g., University of Colorado Boulder, UC Irvine), so this was not blocked by an environment issue. (2) The agent did not produce the required comparison for two courses (provider, rating, estimated duration, level, main skills) and did not recommend the shorter well-rated option. (3) The agent\u2019s own output explicitly states it is unable to complete the task, and it omits the core deliverable (the two-course comparison + recommendation). While the agent claimed duration/rating/level weren\u2019t accessible, screenshots clearly show at least duration (e.g., \u201c6 months at 10 hours a week\u201d) and skills chips for the Google certificate\u2014so even the single-course extraction was under-delivered.\n\nOutcome assessment: From an average user\u2019s perspective, the task was not completed. The user did not receive a two-course attribute comparison nor a justified recommendation, which are the primary deliverables. The agent did avoid enrolling, which is good, but that alone does not satisfy the requested outcome.",
      "output_success": false
    },
